    "containers": {
        "cna": {
            "providerMetadata": {
                "orgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
                "shortName": "Linux",
                "dateUpdated": "2026-11-23T08:07:07.895Z"
            },
            "descriptions": [
                {
                    "lang": "en",
                    "value": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbatman-adv: tt: ignore ROAM flag of received ADD changes\n\nA received TT change (OGM diff or full table response) with the ROAM flag\nbut without DEL is handled by batadv_tt_global_add() like a ROAMING_ADV:\n\n* a newly created global entry gets BATADV_TT_CLIENT_ROAM and is\n  therefore excluded from the global CRC. The sender has it in its local\n  CRC and the receiver has to request the full table again\n* batadv_tt_global_purge_local() removes the local entry of the\n  receiver. The receiver's own client is considered as roamed to the sender\n  and frames for it are rerouted\n\nThe ROAM flag only has a meaning together with DEL. Drop it on reception to\nkeep it from populating the global table with a temporary ROAMING entry\nwhich is not part of the CRC - and therefore causing a CRC mismatch."
                }
            ],
            "metrics": [
                {
                    "cvssV3_1": {
                        "version": "3.1",
                        "vectorString": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:H",
                        "baseScore": 7.6,
                        "baseSeverity": "HIGH"
                    },
                    "scenarios": [
                        {
                            "lang": "en",
                            "value": "AV:A - The BATADV_TT_CLIENT_ROAM bit, without BATADV_TT_CLIENT_DEL, is set in a batadv_tvlv_tt_change carried by an ETH_P_BATMAN OGM (batadv_batman_skb_recv to batadv_iv_ogm_receive or batadv_v_ogm_packet_recv, then batadv_tt_tvlv_ogm_handler_v1) or by a TT_RESPONSE (batadv_recv_unicast_tvlv to batadv_tt_tvlv_unicast_handler_v1). Both enter _batadv_tt_update_changes as L2 mesh frames, so the sender has to be on the batman-adv segment.\nAC:L - The sender puts that flag and its chosen ttvn in the OGM or TT_RESPONSE. batadv_iv_ogm_orig_get creates the orig_node from the OGM, _batadv_tt_update_changes applies the ADD when ttvn is 1 or last_ttvn+1, and batadv_handle_tt_response applies an unsolicited response immediately. A later ADD for the same client takes the existing-entry path in batadv_tt_global_add.\nPR:N - batadv_check_management_packet accepts an OGM that is a broadcast Ethernet frame with a valid source, and batadv_tt_tvlv_unicast_handler_v1 accepts a TT_RESPONSE whose inner destination is a local MAC. Neither handler requires a credential, capability, or signature before calling _batadv_tt_update_changes.\nUI:N - The attacker transmits the OGM or the TT_RESPONSE, which is the only input _batadv_tt_update_changes needs.\nS:U - The affected objects are this node's batadv_tt_global_entry and batadv_tt_local_entry, plus the frames that node already forwards. Those remain under the same kernel batman-adv authority.\nC:L - batadv_transtable_search returns the sender that batadv_tt_global_add stored for the client MAC in the TT change, and batadv_check_unicast_ttvn calls batadv_reroute_unicast_packet to forward that client's unicast frames to the sender. The disclosure is those forwarded frames, not kernel memory.\nI:L - batadv_tt_global_add ORs in the ROAM flag and batadv_tt_global_del_orig_list replaces the originator list of that one client with the sender. batadv_tt_local_remove marks only the matching local entry ROAM and PENDING, which batadv_tt_local_commit_changes later drops. The write is confined to those TT entries and the rewritten unicast dest.\nA:H - batadv_tt_local_remove marks the matching local client BATADV_TT_CLIENT_ROAM and PENDING, so batadv_is_my_client fails and batadv_check_unicast_ttvn forwards its unicast to the attacker. batadv_tt_local_commit_changes then deletes the local entry. Re-sending the TT change after the client reappears in batadv_tt_local_add keeps that delivery denied."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ],
