                {
                    "lang": "en",
                    "value": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: L2CAP: Reject signalling responses in invalid states\n\nA peer can send configuration messages while an\nincoming channel is in BT_CONNECT2, before the\nsecurity or deferred accept gate has completed. A\nconfiguration response can then promote the channel\nto BT_CONNECTED. Configuration responses can also\nact on channels that are closing, and a late connection\nresponse can move a disconnecting channel back to\nBT_CONFIG.\n\nAccept connection responses only while waiting in\nBT_CONNECT. Answer configuration requests in\nBT_CONNECT2, but defer our own request until\nBT_CONFIG so configuration cannot complete before\nthe gate. Ignore configuration responses outside\nBT_CONFIG and BT_CONNECTED, and only complete\nconfiguration in BT_CONFIG."
                }
            ],
            "metrics": [
                {
                    "cvssV3_1": {
                        "version": "3.1",
                        "vectorString": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:L",
                        "baseScore": 8.3,
                        "baseSeverity": "HIGH"
                    },
                    "scenarios": [
                        {
                            "lang": "en",
                            "value": "AV:A - A remote BR/EDR peer's L2CAP_CONF_REQ, L2CAP_CONF_RSP, and L2CAP_CONN_RSP ride in ACL payloads. hci_acldata_packet() passes them to l2cap_recv_acldata(), l2cap_recv_frame() demuxes signalling CID 0x0001 to l2cap_sig_channel(), and l2cap_bredr_sig_cmd() calls the three patched handlers. Bluetooth radio range makes the vector Adjacent.\nAC:L - The peer clears the LMP_HOST_SSP bit in the remote extended-features page so hci_conn_check_link_mode() does not demand encryption, then sends L2CAP_CONN_REQ while the L2CAP feature-mask exchange is still pending. l2cap_connect() stores that channel as BT_CONNECT2 without l2cap_chan_check_security(). The same peer's CONF_REQ and CONF_RSP then reach l2cap_chan_ready() with no further precondition.\nPR:N - l2cap_bredr_sig_cmd() accepts L2CAP_CONF_REQ, L2CAP_CONF_RSP, and L2CAP_CONN_RSP on the signalling channel before l2cap_chan_check_security() has returned success and before l2cap_security_cfm(). The peer needs no link key, pairing, or local capability.\nUI:N - The peer itself sends the signalling commands. l2cap_config_rsp() calls l2cap_chan_ready() without a userspace read on a FLAG_DEFER_SETUP socket and without anyone answering the HCI authentication request that a failed security check would start.\nS:U - l2cap_chan_ready() sets this host's l2cap_chan and its socket to BT_CONNECTED and delivers SDUs inside that same kernel authority. It does not cross a VM, IOMMU, or other security boundary.\nC:H - After the premature BT_CONNECTED transition, l2cap_data_channel() queues the peer's SDUs to the socket and the service can reply on a channel that never passed l2cap_chan_check_security() or the FLAG_DEFER_SETUP accept in l2cap_sock_recvmsg(). That exposes the protected service's traffic.\nI:H - l2cap_data_channel() accepts the peer's L2CAP data frames once l2cap_chan_ready() has set BT_CONNECTED, so the peer can inject arbitrary service PDUs into a socket whose security or deferred-authorization gate was skipped.\nA:L - l2cap_config_rsp() calls l2cap_ertm_init() whenever CONF_OUTPUT_DONE is set, with no state check. That helper reinitializes tx_q and srej_q with skb_queue_head_init() without purging them, and l2cap_seq_list_init() replaces srej_list.list and retrans_list.list without freeing the old arrays, leaking those objects if configuration is repeated on an ERTM channel."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ],
