    "containers": {
        "cna": {
            "providerMetadata": {
                "orgId": "416baaa9-dc9f-4396-8d5f-8c081fb06d67",
                "shortName": "Linux",
                "dateUpdated": "2026-11-23T08:07:09.138Z"
            },
            "descriptions": [
                {
                    "lang": "en",
                    "value": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbatman-adv: stop originator purge worker before freeing TT\n\nbatadv_mesh_free() releases the translation tables via batadv_tt_free()\nbefore batadv_originator_free() stops orig_work. The purge worker can\ntherefore still run while the TT is torn down. When an originator times\nout, batadv_purge_orig_ref() calls batadv_tt_global_del_orig(), which\nloads tt.global_hash and walks all buckets while taking their locks:\n\n  CPU0                          CPU1\n  batadv_tt_free()              batadv_purge_orig()\n                                  batadv_tt_global_del_orig()\n                                    hash = ...tt.global_hash;\n    batadv_tt_global_table_free()\n      batadv_hash_destroy(hash);\n                                    spin_lock_bh(&hash->list_locks[i]);\n\nDisable orig_work at the beginning of batadv_mesh_free(), directly after\nthe mesh was marked as deactivating. The second\ndisable_delayed_work_sync() in batadv_originator_free() is harmless because\nit is free'd anyway."
                }
            ],
            "metrics": [
                {
                    "cvssV3_1": {
                        "version": "3.1",
                        "vectorString": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H",
                        "baseScore": 7.8,
                        "baseSeverity": "HIGH"
                    },
                    "scenarios": [
                        {
                            "lang": "en",
                            "value": "AV:L - The freed tt.global_hash is destroyed in batadv_mesh_free() after a local RTM_DELLINK: batadv_meshif_destroy_netlink() unregisters the device, netdev_run_todo() calls priv_destructor batadv_meshif_free(), and batadv_tt_free() reaches batadv_hash_destroy() while orig_work can still run batadv_tt_global_del_orig().\nAC:L - The attacker creates the orig_node by injecting an ETH_P_BATMAN OGM on a veth enslaved as a hardif, so batadv_batman_skb_recv() reaches batadv_iv_ogm_orig_get(); after last_seen exceeds 2*BATADV_PURGE_TIMEOUT, batadv_purge_orig_ref() calls batadv_tt_global_del_orig() and the attacker deletes the device during that walk. Extra originators stretch the 1024-bucket loop and the sequence can be repeated.\nPR:L - RTM_NEWLINK/RTM_DELLINK for kind batadv are authorized by CAP_NET_ADMIN in the netns user namespace inside rtnl_link_get_net_capable(); batadv_link_ops and batadv_meshif_init_late() do not require init_net, so unshare(CLONE_NEWUSER|CLONE_NEWNET) can create and destroy the mesh device that runs batadv_mesh_free().\nUI:N - The attacker alone creates the batadv device, enslaves their own veth, sends the OGM that populates orig_hash, and issues the RTM_DELLINK that enters batadv_mesh_free().\nS:U - batadv_tt_global_del_orig() corrupts the host kernel heap, the freed batadv_hashtable and its TT buckets, under the same kernel security authority as the RTM_DELLINK caller.\nC:H - batadv_hash_destroy() kfree()s the hashtable, then batadv_tt_global_del_orig() still loads hash->size, hash->table and hash->list_locks and walks every bucket's hlist. Reclaiming that object lets the attacker aim those fields at kernel memory and read it through the walk.\nI:H - That walk spin_lock_bh()s hash->list_locks[i] and, for each node treated as a batadv_tt_global_entry, batadv_tt_global_del_orig_node() hlist_del_rcu()s the orig_list entry and drops its kref. Attacker-controlled bucket contents are a write and control-flow primitive.\nA:H - spin_lock_bh() on the kfreed list_locks, or an hlist walk of reclaimed table memory inside batadv_tt_global_del_orig(), oopses the kernel. orig_work keeps being queued every BATADV_ORIG_WORK_PERIOD until batadv_originator_free(), so one overlap takes the machine down."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ],
